WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.792 --> 00:00:02.585
OSKAR: So there are a few things
we need to have in mind.

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:04.421
JEFF: Okay.
OSKAR: Before we go in.

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:05.880
So we can see
like the roof here.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.799
JEFF: Yeah.
OSKAR: How thin it is.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.760
And this part can
collapse and it does.

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:13.805
And then inside the ice cave,
you can hear the running water?

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.889
JEFF: I can.

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:15.932
OSKAR: You have
to mind the river.

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:16.891
JEFF: Okay.

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.643
OSKAR: We don't want
to fall in the river.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.978
So one for you, my friend.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.397
JEFF: Thank you, my friend.

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:23.231
Good?

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:24.065
OSKAR: Looking good.
JEFF: I like it.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:27.652
OSKAR: Let's go.
JEFF: Let's do it.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.080
You can hear rocks falling.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.751
There's so much
water just rushing down.

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:48.339
You could just hear pieces of
ice just like falling and, and

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.050
it was cracking.

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:54.012
It was actually a lot
louder than I thought.

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:59.017
I am nervous this
could collapse on me.

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:06.024
But here's the thing.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:09.360
I've had to overcome so
much just to get here.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.489
I can't let my
fears stop me now.

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:15.116
Oh.

00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:17.452
Oh-ho-ho.

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:20.622
This is incredible.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.833
I can't believe how big it is.

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:27.504
OSKAR: It's huge.
JEFF: This is massive.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.883
As I walked through the entrance
and made it past the darkness,

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:35.470
there's just this
massive opening and

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.682
walls of just light
turquoise, kind of blue.

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:41.101
It's glacier blue.

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:42.060
That's what I'm
gonna keep calling it.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.479
Glacier blue sounds great.

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:48.691
To be down here to see the
blue, it's just beautiful.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:49.984
And this is a moulin?

00:01:49.984 --> 00:01:51.986
OSKAR: This is a moulin.

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:53.196
JEFF: And I love it.
It just...

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:56.741
It just continues to look like
somebody like chiseled away.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.662
I've never seen ice this big.

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:04.040
Seeing the ice shaped in all
these crystal-like sculptures

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:05.917
is amazing.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.168
Growing up in Florida,

00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:09.712
I never thought I would
see something like this.

00:02:09.754 --> 00:02:11.673
I'm so excited that
we actually found one.

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:13.842
Really am.

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:16.803
After climbing a glacier,
hiking for miles and

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:20.974
crossing a icy lagoon, to be
here right now is so worth it.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.726
♪ We found a ice cave ♪

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:25.854
♪ We found a ice cave ♪

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:27.981
Yes.

